{
  "format": "sparkbench-project",
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "Pot dimmer",
    "created": "2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z",
    "modified": "2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z",
    "appVersion": "0.1.0",
    "description": "Press Run, then drag the wiper of RV1 up and down while it plays: the LED dims and brightens. The pot divides 9 V; transistor Q1 (emitter follower) copies the wiper voltage minus 0.7 V onto the 330 Ω + LED, so I(LED) ≈ (V(w) − 0.7 − 1.9 V) / 330 Ω: 0 at the bottom, ≈ 6 mA at 50 %, ≈ 19 mA at the top (LED rating 30 mA)."
  },
